
                                                                                Detailed Summary Report

Objective:-

The objective of this week task is to learn Python basics and perform basic data exploration and cleaning using the Pandas library. The task involves -
•	Loading a CSV dataset
•	Exploring the structure
•	Handling missing values
•	Performing filtering and selection operations
•	Removing duplicate records
•	Creating derived columns
•	Saving the cleaned dataset

Steps Performed:-

•	Loaded the CSV dataset into a Pandas DataFrame using pd.read_csv().
•	Explored the dataset using head(), tail(), shape, columns, and dtypes.
•	Identified missing values using isnull().sum() and handled them using fillna() or dropna().
•	Performed basic operations such as filtering rows and selecting columns.
•	Removed duplicate rows using drop_duplicates().
•	Created a derived column such as total_amount = initial_price *rating.
•	Saved the cleaned dataset into a new CSV file using to_csv().

Conclusion:-

This task helped in understanding the basics of Python and Pandas for data analysis and preprocessing. 
